cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "certainty-scan: an evidence-sufficiency instrument for project work items"
abstract: >-
  A command-line instrument that scores each work item in an issue tracker on
  how much of the evidence that would justify confidence actually exists, and
  reports what is missing. Five signals — validation, dependencies, acceptance
  criteria, evidence structure, and recorded decisions — combine into a 0-100
  score per item. Scoring is deterministic and performs no model inference.
  Three anti-circularity rules prevent the tool, or the automation it measures,
  from raising its own score. A sealed-reveal protocol supports blind comparison
  of machine scores against an independent expert rating.
